// Monsters and bosses for the monster lookup, in the Pixel Remaster's names (the wiki's main
// names; "alt" is the SNES name). GBA-only enemies (Dragons' Den, Soul Shrine, GBA espers) and
// unused ("dummied") enemies are left out.
//
// Sources:
//   - Final Fantasy Wiki enemy pages (category "Enemies in Final Fantasy VI" and "Bosses in
//     Final Fantasy VI"), https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Enemies_in_Final_Fantasy_VI
//     Text from the wiki is available under CC BY-SA 3.0, and so is this adapted data. Steals,
//     drops and abilities use the wiki's GBA fields, whose names match the Pixel Remaster.
//   - Common or rare steal and drop odds: Gamer Corner's FF6 monster table
//     (https://gamercorner.net/ffvi/monsters/), matched by SNES name, falling back to the
//     wiki's slot order.
//   - Bestiary numbers ("b"): the Pixel Remaster Gau Rage Checklist (see rages-data.js).
//   - Pictures: sprites hosted on the Final Fantasy Wiki. "img" is a path under IMG_BASE. They
//     are loaded from the wiki (without a referrer, which the wiki requires) and never copied
//     into this repository.
//
// Fields: name, alt, boss, b, img, and either the stats below or forms: [{ name, ...stats }].
// Stats: level, hp, mp, exp, gil, el { weak, absorb, immune, resist }, imm (status
// immunities), traits, steal and drop ([[item, "common" | "rare" | "always"]]), special,
// other, rage, sketch, control, where.

